td 2026-08-06: FROZEN-SOURCE TAKES root-caused by measurement, not by guessing (PO: "recorded in Chrome, switched to a tab with a game, nothing was recorded, just frozen frame"). Built a real-Chrome probe (Chrome 150 / macOS 26, genuinely backgrounded tab, remote-debugging driven — the in-app preview browser is NOT a valid harness: it runs with backgrounding disabled and reports hidden while still rendering at full rate). Measured, hidden tab, rAF at 0/s: AudioWorklet tick 63/s, canvas.captureStream(30) 30fps, captureStream(0)+requestFrame 63/s, detached <video>(MediaStream)→drawImage ~56/s, MediaRecorder ~110 KB/s — EVERY link of the live-composite chain survives backgrounding, so the composite does not freeze and a frozen file means the SOURCE stopped. Two more measurements that shaped the fix: a tab under capture never goes hidden at all (Chrome force-renders it, so self/tab-capture takes are immune), and a completely static surface still yields ~1 keep-alive frame/s — therefore "no frame for 3s" is dead, not idle, and is a safe stall threshold. Shipped (all additive, PO frozen rule respected — nothing that worked was removed): (1) src/core/capture/sourceLiveness.ts, a pure unit-tested detector fed from the composite's AudioWorklet tick (never rAF — the tab IS backgrounded when this happens) emitting stalled/resumed edges off the source's media clock; (2) session emits channel-stalled/channel-resumed, records Recording.stalled, and marks the composite UNUSABLE rather than cancelling it (it keeps running so it keeps watching; doStop cancels it and reclaims the encoder/audio-context/orphan blob — a leak the old skip-path had) so an unedited export renders from the raw channels instead of copying still frames; (3) the same treatment when a video track ENDS mid-take — a real bug: the dead track keeps readyState 2, so the composite repainted its last frame for the rest of the take and instant export copied it verbatim; (4) sticky red capture banner, because a toast is